##19th of October, 2025

I am reading a book called: Inner Excellence. One of the main arguments in this book is that we should not focus on the result, instead, we should focus on the progress. And I adotped this logic into my archery training perfectly. 

Why shouldn't we focus on the result? You may ask. The problem is that, the result doesn't corrolate to your performace. 